Z||000002||V8Fiero||05-28-2001||12:01 AM||||code 32<P>"the EGR solenoid should not be energized and vacuum should not pass to the EGR valve" The dianostic switch should close at about 2 inches of vacuum. With vacuum applied, the switch should close. Replace the EGR valve."<P>code 35<P>Code 35 will set when a closed throttle speed is 50 rpm above or below the correct idle speed for 30 secs. Replace the IAC"<P>Could somebody please explain this in better terms for me.........<P>Thanks.<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-28-2001||12:12 AM||||code 13,  open oxygen sensor circuit.  If the  o2 sensor is plugged in than replace it.<P>code 32,  EGR system failure. The cause for mine was a vacuum leak-rotten vacuum resivior<P>code 35,  Idle air control. Idle is higher than ECM allows and ECM can not get it any lower. Probable cause is vacuum leak.<P>code 44,  lean exhaust indicated. pobable due to vacuum leak or malfunctioning  o2 sensor.<P>So get a vacuum guage and check vacuum lines at different areas before controlers/soliniods. should be around 18.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPete.jpg"> ||||reg||1
